  "plan": {
    "target": "Missing mstateen0.ENVCFG Gating on senvcfg (CSR 0x10A) Access and Execution Controls in Supervisor Mode (src/privileged/csrc.sv, src/privileged/privdec.sv, src/privileged/csr.sv, src/ieu/controller.sv)",
    "rationale": "Under the RISC-V State Enable ('Smstateen') Extension Specification (Ratified, Sections 1 and 2), bit 62 of mstateen0 controls access to the environment configuration state (ENVCFG). When mstateen0[62] is 0 (disabled by Machine mode), any attempt by a less privileged mode (Supervisor or User mode) to access senvcfg (CSR 0x10A) or senvcfgh must raise an illegal instruction exception (mcause = 2). Furthermore, any execution controls governed by senvcfg (such as CBZE for cbo.zero in Zicboz) must behave as if disabled (or raise an illegal instruction exception). In CORE-V Wally, src/privileged/privdec.sv and src/privileged/csrc.sv decode and permit accesses to senvcfg solely based on privilege level (PrivilegeMode >= S) without gating on mstateen0[62]. Consequently, when M-mode leaves mstateen0[62] = 0, S-mode can execute csrr/csrw to senvcfg and execute cache-block operations (cbo.zero) without taking the mandatory illegal instruction trap. Standard architectural tests (riscv-arch-test) do not stress cross-privilege stateen disable transitions before executing S-mode CSR accesses or Zicboz instructions. Previous attempts at this target were exhausted by operational test infrastructure mistakes (Spike timeout due to missing _start/entry point at 0x80000000, followed by shell redirection forbidden at the reproducer boundary), leaving the underlying RTL bug confirmed present and unaddressed.",
    "tester_prompt": "Investigate and construct a differential reproducer for missing mstateen0[62] (ENVCFG) gating on S-mode senvcfg access and Zicboz execution.\n\n1. Target RTL & Configuration:\n   - Modules: src/privileged/csrc.sv, src/privileged/privdec.sv, src/privileged/csr.sv, src/ieu/controller.sv\n   - Configuration: rv64gc with smstateen and zicboz enabled.\n   - Signals: CSR decode logic for CSR 0x10A (senvcfg), mstateen0 register output bit 62 (ENVCFG), and privilege mode signals (PrivilegeMode).\n\n2. Hypothesized Failure:\n   - When mstateen0[62] == 0, S-mode reads or writes to CSR 0x10A (senvcfg) fail to raise an illegal instruction exception in Wally, whereas Spike correctly raises an illegal instruction trap (mcause = 2).\n   - Furthermore, execution of cbo.zero in S-mode with mstateen0[62] == 0 executes without trapping in Wally, while Spike raises an illegal instruction exception.\n\n3. Critical Test Construction Rules (DO NOT REPEAT PREVIOUS PITFALLS):\n   - Linker Script & Entry Point: The test ELF MUST have entry point `_start` mapped to `0x80000000` (e.g., using a proper linker script with `.text.init` at 0x80000000). Spike boots at 0x1000 and jumps directly to 0x80000000. If `_start` is missing or code is located at 0x10000, Spike will spin in an infinite trap loop and hit the 900-second deadline.\n   - HTIF tohost / fromhost: Define `.section .tohost, \"aw\", @progbits` with `.balign 64`, `.globl tohost, fromhost`, and terminate by writing `1` ((0 << 1) | 1) to `tohost` on PASS, or `3` ((1 << 1) | 1) on FAIL.\n   - Reproducer Contract (`reproducer.json`):\n     * Never use shell control flow or redirection (`>`, `<`, `|`, `&&`, `;`) in `reproducer.json` fields.\n     * Place all GCC compilation commands inside an executable script: `${TEST_DIR}/build_reproducer.sh`.\n     * `reproducer.json` must specify: `\"version\": 1`, `\"oracle\": \"spike\"`, `\"build\": [\"${TEST_DIR}/build_reproducer.sh\"]`, `\"control\": {\"mode\": \"selfcheck\", \"wally\": [\"${WALLY}/bin/wsim\", \"rv64gc\", \"--sim\", \"verilator\", \"--elf\", \"${TEST_DIR}/build/control.elf\"], \"oracle\": [\"/usr/bin/spike\", \"--isa=rv64gc_smstateen_zicboz\", \"+signature=${TEST_DIR}/logs/control-spike.sig\", \"+signature-granularity=8\", \"${TEST_DIR}/build/control.elf\"], \"oracle_signature\": \"logs/control-spike.sig\"}`, and a corresponding `\"test\"` block pointing to `build/test.elf` and `logs/test-spike.sig`.\n     * Register trap vector symbols in `\"trap_vectors\"`: `[{\"elf\": \"build/control.elf\", \"symbol\": \"trap_handler\"}, {\"elf\": \"build/test.elf\", \"symbol\": \"trap_handler\"}]`.\n\n4. Directed Test Plan:\n   - `control.S` (Positive Control - must PASS on both Spike and Wally):\n     1. Boot in M-mode, setup mtvec to `trap_handler`, configure PMP (pmpaddr0 = -1, pmpcfg0 = 0x1F) to allow all memory accesses.\n     2. Set `mstateen0[62] = 1` (enable ENVCFG).\n     3. Set `menvcfg.CBZE = 1` (bit 7) and `senvcfg.CBZE = 1` (bit 7).\n     4. Switch to S-mode via `mret` (mstatus.MPP = 1, mepc = smode_entry).\n     5. In S-mode: read `senvcfg` into a register and verify no trap occurs; execute `cbo.zero` on a scratch buffer.\n     6. If no trap occurs, write `1` to `tohost` (wg_pass).\n     7. Trap handler records failure (tohost = 3) if an unexpected trap occurs.\n   - `test.S` (Negative / Reproducer Test - passes on Spike oracle, FAILS on buggy Wally RTL):\n     1. Boot in M-mode, setup mtvec to `trap_handler`, configure PMP.\n     2. Clear `mstateen0[62] = 0` (ENVCFG disabled for lower modes).\n     3. Set `menvcfg.CBZE = 1` (bit 7) and set mepc to smode_entry, then `mret` to enter S-mode.\n     4. In S-mode: attempt to access `senvcfg` (`csrr t1, 0x10A`) or execute `cbo.zero (a0)`.\n     5. Expected Oracle Behavior (Spike): S-mode generates an Illegal Instruction trap (mcause = 2). The trap handler catches mcause == 2, verifies mepc points to the offending instruction, records success, and exits with `tohost = 1` (PASS).\n     6. Buggy DUT Behavior (Wally RTL): Wally fails to raise an illegal instruction trap; execution falls through without trapping. The test code following the S-mode access detects that no trap was raised and exits with `tohost = 3` (FAIL).\n\n5. Validation:\n   - Run `architect_a8231c588f_validate_reproducer` on `${TEST_DIR}/reproducer.json` before submitting to ensure the contract is schema-compliant.",
    "knowledge": "1. RISC-V State Enable ('Smstateen') Specification (Ratified, Sections 1 & 2):\n   - Defines CSRs mstateen0..3 (0x30C..0x30F), mstateen0h..3h (0x31C..0x31F), hstateen0..3, and sstateen0..3.\n   - Bit 62 of mstateen0 is ENVCFG. When mstateen0[62] == 0, attempts to access senvcfg (0x10A), senvcfgh (0x11A), henvcfg (0x60A), or henvcfgh (0x61A) in privilege modes less than M-mode MUST raise an illegal instruction exception (mcause = 2).\n   - Furthermore, any execution controls governed by senvcfg (such as CBZE bit 7 for cbo.zero in Zicboz) must act as disabled/zero or raise an illegal instruction exception.\n\n2. Wally Source Code Findings:\n   - `src/privileged/csrc.sv`: Defines CSR read/write multiplexing and access registers.\n   - `src/privileged/privdec.sv`: Privilege instruction and CSR decode logic. Access permissions are checked using privilege level (`PrivilegeMode >= S` for 0x10A) without gating on `mstateen0[62]`.\n   - `src/ieu/controller.sv`: Instruction execution unit controller. Zicboz execution checks menvcfg/senvcfg CBZE bits but does not verify that ENVCFG is enabled in mstateen0.\n\n3. Test Environment & Harness Lessons from History:\n   - Spike reset vector is 0x1000 and immediately jumps to 0x80000000. All test ELFs must define `_start` and place `.text.init` at 0x80000000 via a dedicated linker script.\n   - Omitting `_start` or placing code at 0x10000 causes Spike to hit uninitialized memory at 0x80000000, triggering an infinite trap loop that expires the 900s timeout.\n   - `reproducer.json` does NOT allow shell syntax or redirection (`>`, `&&`, `|`). All build steps must be wrapped inside an executable shell script (e.g. `build_reproducer.sh`).\n   - Selfcheck termination requires writing `(exit_code << 1) | 1` to `tohost` in `.tohost` section (`1` for pass, `3` for fail)."
  },
