        "report": "The baseline reproducer failed due to a host command timeout on Spike (900 seconds). This occurs because standard RISC-V architectural tests execute from 0x80000000, whereas Spike initially boots from its ROM at 0x1000. Without a linker script explicitly placing `.text.init` at `0x80000000` alongside an entry point jump wrapper, execution hits an infinite uninitialized memory trap loop on Spike. To rectify this, the included build procedure dynamically writes an appropriate `linker.ld`, explicitly locates `_start` at `0x80000000` via `.text.init`, and properly aligns `.tohost` and `scratch` sections. The test programs check the architectural requirement of `mstateen0` bit 62: when `mstateen0[62]==0` (disabled) and S-mode accesses `senvcfg`, Spike correctly routes an illegal instruction exception (mcause=2), which the S-mode trap handler maps to a `tohost=1` PASS condition. Conversely, CORE-V Wally fails to enforce the `mstateen0` gating, does not trap, and incorrectly falls through to `tohost=3` FAIL condition. The python build shim is constructed to bypass environment shell lockups and writes `build_reproducer.sh` and the source assembly explicitly before invoking compilation.",
